      "message": "feat(Navier-Stokes): formalization of Navier–Stokes existence and smoothness (#1457)\n\nfixes #2293\n\nFormalization of Navier-Stokes existence and smoothness problem as\ndescribed in\nhttps://www.claymath.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/navierstokes.pdf\n\nPotentially issues:\n- not immediately obvious that `fderiv ℝ (v · t) x (v x t)` is the\nconvective term and that `div` is divergence\n- the growth conditions uses `‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ n v₀ x‖` instead of\n`|∂^α u(x,t)|` but it should be equivalent\n- at various places I'm not completely sure if there should be `t ≥ 0`\nor `t > 0` as `fderiv` might not give what we think at `t=0`. Mainly in\n`NavierStokesExistenceAndSmoothness.navierStokes`\n\nNote:\n- I didn't use the unicode character nu for viscosity as it looks too\nsimilar to the letter `v` which is used for velocity.\n- bikeshead: should it use `v(x,t)`(aligned with the official statement)\nor `v(t,x)` that is more mathlib aligned?\n- should it be formulated in an arbitrary dimension and then\ninstantiated for `n:=3`?\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Paul Lezeau <[redacted-address CORRECTIONS.md §80]>\nCo-authored-by: Paul Lezeau <[redacted-address CORRECTIONS.md §80]>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "f7a3dcc0573b5390310c0a858f0b2058e833ee6b",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/git/trees/f7a3dcc0573b5390310c0a858f0b2058e833ee6b"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/git/commits/641ff32207fdcf4fdf6aeda4dbb02f6d9be0c251",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqB4eqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8ecQAB8u7aYsmIzKueyHDBRz8JBP\nBZPcUYA7F14Sa4+BJWRXcXYdKZQ/lFTOJVtuzCQ3Y+QnRmiOkNzQamSqRxZhf80T\nTmdSwIanBSH6L4+4EXp9YSdt0oa4uMkAmXm5gf0c9MRkJ4JutVWGRfdLkyWusH66\n+DYPq+uxQsfeGbUo8jNWYsuiIuNHx3VUSyhzMBBB9GWX9OEniGer/E2dOMR8UIYm\nfAFBEOdlCfyVvhbWPytfgIxOCOwFGhU1XLGWeaZSwWwjzUrJQ9KTmGc1Qlxc/SRp\nYj4pRefNmGC9SQf76B8UKASK7mb/st4Ol6aNVHo/RXt7RN3i7G6DYJi6Y0wTBBzA\nYHyYm7Ol6nAvH+Xb0BJILBYlziraQPoD736seUJWVo0kWnum8Rl5Uj0iTt9/DRQ4\n0z4siLe9p377M+4HrDfHD/Cn05P06S2DyBCrMtDfrQ5+bjhhIPCcBojoJz8ItoMS\ny0ypjKETLGtE55fL/ttmVW34BCmynAWseCbC456Ui9tdMOw0pCIefRhs1D3cgSMX\njD2SwiShSHOpz436IShLGj+6i3Ilg535dIeqw7t/Fg+JK6UxeAekP5lUHwSw0QpM\nglg2213eeARIfvadd/1FbWCFjARkh7E8lB9sEx0nttICS5gfArtVR0CovjZ1GB83\ncJA15e7TsdfG38cNaMbq\n=UujU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree f7a3dcc0573b5390310c0a858f0b2058e833ee6b\nparent 9cd163460111a40e44953de77ab7de9efef903a9\nauthor Tomáš Skřivan <[redacted-address CORRECTIONS.md §80]> 1778878378 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778878378 +0000\n\nfeat(Navier-Stokes): formalization of Navier–Stokes existence and smoothness (#1457)\n\nfixes #2293\n\nFormalization of Navier-Stokes existence and smoothness problem as\ndescribed in\nhttps://www.claymath.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/navierstokes.pdf\n\nPotentially issues:\n- not immediately obvious that `fderiv ℝ (v · t) x (v x t)` is the\nconvective term and that `div` is divergence\n- the growth conditions uses `‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ n v₀ x‖` instead of\n`|∂^α u(x,t)|` but it should be equivalent\n- at various places I'm not completely sure if there should be `t ≥ 0`\nor `t > 0` as `fderiv` might not give what we think at `t=0`. Mainly in\n`NavierStokesExistenceAndSmoothness.navierStokes`\n\nNote:\n- I didn't use the unicode character nu for viscosity as it looks too\nsimilar to the letter `v` which is used for velocity.\n- bikeshead: should it use `v(x,t)`(aligned with the official statement)\nor `v(t,x)` that is more mathlib aligned?\n- should it be formulated in an arbitrary dimension and then\ninstantiated for `n:=3`?\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Paul Lezeau <[redacted-address CORRECTIONS.md §80]>\nCo-authored-by: Paul Lezeau <[redacted-address CORRECTIONS.md §80]>",
